comments.body:
@Johnny Bieren to support multiple CPEs we have to restructure RPA schema and allow user to set CPE for a group of components. In theory CPE per component can work as well, because at the end of the day it's product variant to component mapping. But I think it would be more user friendly to allow user to set CPE stream per group of components.
The same information has to be replicated to the advisory of course and that will require in-advance notice to ProdSec tooling team to support it correctly, because based on CPE and component we create CSAF files.
As for now we were able to release everything without this feature, only people who use RHEL 8 and RHEL 9 images in the same product stream had to create two RPAs instead of one, which is not great customer experience, but also it's not the end of the world. RHEL Team who mostly used that functionality in the legacy pipelines agreed to use separate RPAs for different product variants, so there is no pressure.

