Currently we require that each Konflux advisory fixes exactly one product. So we'll need a data model change (add ForeignKey from one KonfluxVariant to many KonfluxContainers, remove ForeignKey from one KonfluxVariant to many KonfluxAdvisories) just to support loading these advisories. This is true even if we don't support using them for anything / generating CSAF files or other data from them.
We have a "cpes" property on the KonfluxAdvisory model. This needs to iterate over the linked set of variants, instead of assuming there's only one variant. Which means we need to know "which containers relate to which variants / CPEs?" when reading each advisory's data:
@cached_property
def cpes(self):
    cpe_pkgs = set()
    for container in self.konfluxcontainer_set.get_queryset():
        # container.purl uses the custom_purl field directly if set
        # If custom_purl is empty, this property will build the correct purl for us
        purl = PackageURL.from_string(container.purl)
        cpe_pkgs.add(f"{self.variant.cpe}/{purl.name}")

    return sorted(cpe_pkgs)
